---
import Snippet from '../../components/docs/Snippet.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const refdes = 'text-accent m-0 mb-4 font-mono text-sm font-normal tracking-normal';

const launcherScaffold = `bun create bridgething my-hub --launcher`;

const launcherManifest = `{
  "id": "…",
  "name": "My Hub",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "role": "launcher"
}`;

const launcherSdk = `// the daemon hides launcher-role bundles from this list
const list = await client.webapp.list();
const current = await client.webapp.current();

const icon = await client.webapp.icon({ id: info.id });
await client.webapp.activate({ id: info.id });

// redraw when a webapp is installed or removed
client.webapp.onWebappInstalled(reload);
client.webapp.onWebappUninstalled(reload);`;

const overlayScaffold = `bun create bridgething my-overlay --overlay`;

const overlayManifest = `{
  "id": "…",
  "name": "My Overlay",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "overlay": "overlay.js"
}`;

const overlayGlobal = `// the daemon prepends this before your bundle
window.__bridgethingOverlay = {
  origin: 'http://127.0.0.1:8891',
  surfaces: {
    notifications: true,
    call: true,
    pairing: true,
    connection: true,
    voice: true,
    volume: false, // this webapp draws its own volume indicator
  },
};`;

const overlayOptOut = `{
  "id": "…",
  "name": "My App",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "overlays": {
    "volume": false,
    "notifications": false
  }
}`;

const overlayBoot = `const cfg = window.__bridgethingOverlay;
if (!cfg || !location.origin.startsWith(cfg.origin)) return; // not a page the daemon served
if (window.__bridgethingOverlayMounted) return;               // double injection is a no-op
window.__bridgethingOverlayMounted = true;

if (cfg.surfaces.volume) wireVolume(client);
if (cfg.surfaces.pairing) wirePairing(client);`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="launchers and overlays"
  description="build your own home screen for the device's launcher slot, and your own system overlay."
  current="launchers-and-overlays">
  <header class="mb-12">
    <h1>launchers and overlays</h1>
    <p class="text-white/60">the hub and the system overlay are webapps.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="mb-14">
    <h2 class={refdes}>s1 - two slots</h2>
    <p class="text-white/60">a slot names one installed bundle for a system role:</p>
    <ul role="list" class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-white/60">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white/80">launcher.</strong> the home screen. press the menu button 5 times to reach it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white/80">overlay.</strong> the ui drawn on top of every webapp: notification toasts, the call
        banner, the pairing pin, the disconnected banner, the voice indicator, and the volume indicator.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-white/60">you set both from the companion app. an empty slot uses the built-in one.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-14">
    <h2 class={refdes}>s2 - what every webapp gets for free</h2>
    <p class="text-white/60">
      overlays default <strong class="text-white/80">on</strong>. a webapp that declares nothing gets all six.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-white/60">
      turn one off in the manifest's <code>overlays</code> block when you draw it yourself. an omitted key stays on, so list
      only what you take over.
    </p>
    <Snippet code={overlayOptOut} lang="json" />
    <p class="mt-3 text-white/60">
      the six keys are <code>notifications</code>, <code>call</code>, <code>pairing</code>, <code>connection</code>,
      <code>voice</code>, and <code>volume</code>. a key gates the drawn ui only; the events still reach your webapp.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-14">
    <h2 class={refdes}>s3 - build a launcher</h2>
    <Snippet code={launcherScaffold} lang="bash" />
    <p class="mt-3 text-white/60">
      <code>"role": "launcher"</code> hides the bundle from <code>client.webapp.list</code> and makes it eligible for the
      launcher slot.
    </p>
    <Snippet code={launcherManifest} lang="json" />
    <p class="mt-3 text-white/60">everything a home screen needs is on the normal client:</p>
    <Snippet code={launcherSdk} />
    <p class="mt-3 text-white/60">
      the built-in hub also handles bluetooth bonds and the pairing name, display brightness, system health, power, and
      ota progress.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-14">
    <h2 class={refdes}>s4 - build an overlay</h2>
    <Snippet code={overlayScaffold} lang="bash" />
    <Snippet code={overlayManifest} lang="json" />
    <p class="mt-3 text-white/60">
      while your bundle holds the overlay slot, the daemon injects <code>overlay.js</code> into every webapp's document as
      it loads.
    </p>
    <Snippet code={overlayGlobal} />
    <p class="mt-3 text-white/60">
      <strong class="text-white/80">honor <code>surfaces</code>.</strong> draw only what its keys allow, or the screen shows
      that ui twice.
    </p>
    <Snippet code={overlayBoot} />
    <ul role="list" class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-white/60">
      <li><strong class="text-white/80">origin guard.</strong> run only in a page the daemon served.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white/80">mount guard.</strong> a second injection must do nothing.</li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white/80">closed shadow root.</strong> it keeps your styles and the webapp's apart.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white/80">escape-only, capture-phase keys.</strong> bind them only while something is showing.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/60">
      <code>overlay.js</code> must be <strong class="text-white/80">one self-contained file</strong> under 512&nbsp;KiB.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class={refdes}>s5 - assign it, and get back</h2>
    <p class="text-white/60">install the bundle, then pick it in the companion app under home screen or overlay.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-white/60">to get back to the built-in:</p>
    <ul role="list" class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-white/60">
      <li><strong class="text-white/80">clear the slot</strong> in the companion app.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white/80">uninstall the bundle</strong></li>
      <li><strong class="text-white/80">factory reset</strong></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
